                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#CollapsingContractibleSubcomplexes"} Collapsing contractible subcomplexes
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            %em CW-pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,A)
            is meant a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with a sub-complex inclusion
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
          %p
            The concept appears prominently in the discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+homology"} relative homology
            and generally in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Steenrod+axioms"} Eilenberg-Steenrod axioms
            for
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology"} generalized homology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology"} generalized cohomology
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complex"} CW complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              of any subcomplex has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              which is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+retract"} deformation retract
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %em
                %a{:href => "relative+homology#GoodPair"} good pair
              in the sense of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+homology"} relative homology
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher02"}> Hatcher 2002, prop. A.5
            ).
          #HomologyOfQuotientSpace.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,A)
              a CW-pair, then the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+singular+homology"} relative singular homology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              coincides with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+singular+homology"} reduced singular homology
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_n(X , A)
                    \\simeq
                    \\tilde H_n(X/A)
                    \\,.
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher02"}> Hatcher 2002, prop. 2.22
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By assumption we can find a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi j
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{j}{\to} U \hookrightarrow X
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow U
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+retract"} deformation retract
              and hence in particular is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              and so induces also isomorphisms on all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
              groups.
            %p
              It follows in particular that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              the canonical morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi id
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n(X,A) \stackrel{H_n(id,j)}{\to} H_n(X,U)
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %a{:href => "relative+homology#HomotopyInvariance"} homotopy invariance
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+singular+homology"} relative singular homology
            %p
              Given such
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              we have an evident
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of pairs of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
