            %p
              Here the left horizontal morphisms are the above isomorphims induced from the deformation retract. The right horizontal morphisms are isomorphisms by
              %a{:href => "relative%20homology#Excision"} excision
              and the right vertical morphism is an isomorphism since it is induced by a homeomorphism. Hence the left vertical morphism is an isomorphism (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-3"} 2-out-of-3
              for isomorphisms).
          %h3#CollapsingContractibleSubcomplexes Collapsing contractible subcomplexes
          %p
          #Pinching.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              If the sub-complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+homotopy+type"} contractible
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quotient+space"} quotient
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coprojection"} coprojection
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ∼
                    %mi A
                    %mphantom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mphantom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ∼
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\ast \overset{\sim}{\longrightarrow} A
                    \\phantom{---}
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \\phantom{---}
                    X \overset{\sim}{\longrightarrow} X/A
                    \\,.
            %p
          (e.g.
          %a{:href => "#Hatcher02"} Hatcher 02
          = succeed ")." do
            %a{:href => "https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/AT.pdf#page=20"} p 11
          %p
          #SphereWithArcAttached.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              (in
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset X
              — to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
            .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 20px 10px"}
              %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
                %img{:src => "/nlab/files/PinchingSphereAtTwoPoints.png", :width => "300px"}/
                %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                  (from
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "#Hatcher02"} Hatcher 2002
